2. Framer Motion vs Framer (the website builder)
These are actually two different things! Framer Motion is just a React animation library—totally compatible with coding your own site. You'd install it like any other package (npm install framer-motion) and write animations in code. Great skill to learn. Framer (the website builder) is the no-code tool—not what you'd use here.

3. Contact Form
Don't overcomplicate it. EmailJS is the move—free tier, takes ~20 minutes to set up, form submissions go straight to your inbox. No backend, no database, just a few lines of JS. Storing locally (like a JSON file) isn't really how websites work since your server resets. EmailJS is the right call.

4. Checking your GitHub Student Pack domain
Go to education.github.com/pack → sign in → search "domain". You likely have access to a free .me domain via Namecheap, or possibly .dev via another provider. Takes 2 minutes to check!

